{
 "description": "Shared cases for InterviewPrep::PracticeTaskFence (Rails) and database/interview_questions.py (Python). Each case saves one task command next to a small set of rows, then both sides say whether the task is still current. expect.rails is 'current' or the fence's stale reason; expect.python is 'current' or 'stale'. Where the two sides differ on purpose, the 'note' says why. Rails checks at apply time (task running, newest of its type); Python checks at read time (task must be queued).",
 "placeholders": "'@set' and '@q1'..'@q5' in commands stand for saved ids. q1 is the task subject; q2..q5 are its peers. A case's 'command_changes' edits the base command (null removes a key). Other overrides: 'set' changes the set row, 'questions' changes or drops (null) rows, 'retired' retires a row, 'no_questions' empties the set, 'newer_task' adds a newer task of the same type, 'task_status' sets the task status, 'task_owner' = 'other_user' queues the task for another user, 'subject' points the task at another record.",
